# Project agent layout

- Skills live in `.cursor/skills/` (version-controlled). Activate the matching skill when working in that domain.
- Project rules live in `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` (version-controlled). Follow every rule whose globs cover files you are about to change.
- Do not recreate `.agents/skills` or `.ai/rules` for this project. If Boost regenerates skills under `.agents/`, move them into `.cursor/skills/` and prefer `.cursor`.
- `composer require` / `composer update` must **not** run `boost:update`. That command stays out of `post-update-cmd`. Run `php artisan boost:update` only when a human deliberately wants Boost's stock guidelines or skills refreshed, then review the diff before committing.
- Never run `php artisan boost:install`. Boost is installed already, and the installer rewrites `AGENTS.md` and its own skills from scratch. `CLAUDE.md` says so too, because the stock Laravel README section still tells agents to run it.
- **`AGENTS.md` has two halves.** Boost replaces everything between `<laravel-boost-guidelines>` and `</laravel-boost-guidelines>` on every update; the `# Michicast House Rules` section below the closing marker is hand-written and survives. Put project guidance there, never inside the block. That split is why `boost.json` can keep `"guidelines": true`.
- **Never hand-edit a Boost-provided skill** (`infer-conventions`, `laravel-best-practices`, `testing-best-practices`, `tailwindcss-development`). They are copied fresh from the package on every update, and `boost.json`'s `skills` array is regenerated *output* rather than an input filter, so removing a name does not protect the file. Override stock text from `.cursor/rules` instead: `cruddy-by-design.mdc` overrides `laravel-best-practices`, and this file overrides `infer-conventions` — record conventions as `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`, never `.ai/rules`, and do not call `record-rule`. `BOOST_RULES_ENABLED=false` keeps Boost from emitting its own competing `.ai/rules` section. House-owned skills (`ship-issue`, `create-github-issue`) are not Boost skills and stay out of that array so Boost's stale-skill pruning cannot delete them.
- Durable project decisions belong in `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` with YAML frontmatter (`description`, `globs`, `alwaysApply`).
- Local MCP secrets stay in `.cursor/mcp.json` (gitignored). Copy from `.cursor/mcp.example.json`.
